      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "2 Days in the Valley emerged during the post-<a href=\"/movie/680\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"680\">Pulp Fiction</a> (1994) wave of multi-narrative crime films, weaving together interconnected stories across Los Angeles' San Fernando Valley. Director John Herzfeld crafts a darkly comic thriller that shares DNA with <a href=\"/movie/695\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"695\">Short Cuts</a> (1993) and <a href=\"/movie/334\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"334\">Magnolia</a> (1999), but with a sharper criminal edge. The film launched Charlize Theron's career and featured a stellar ensemble including James Spader, Danny Aiello, and Jeff Daniels. Its sun-bleached Valley locations and sardonic tone perfectly capture mid-90s LA noir."
      },
